WEBVTT

00:36.619 --> 00:38.121
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

00:38.955 --> 00:40.165
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

01:36.638 --> 01:39.849
The air is so hot, it's hard to breathe.

01:40.433 --> 01:44.479
So this is the outside of the outside

01:44.562 --> 01:45.897
the teacher was talking about?

01:47.190 --> 01:49.067
Is this the test?

01:49.150 --> 01:50.276
If it is,

01:50.360 --> 01:54.155
at least the teachers can't be mad
at us for coming here.

01:54.239 --> 01:55.240
You're right.

01:55.740 --> 01:57.367
Should we go get the others?

01:57.450 --> 02:00.203
No. Let's take a look first.

02:00.286 --> 02:02.163
If this really is the test,

02:02.247 --> 02:04.833
who goes first will probably
count towards our grades.

02:05.417 --> 02:08.003
So what are we looking for?

02:08.086 --> 02:11.423
Look. The wire fence is broken over there.

02:12.007 --> 02:14.759
That means there must be
another outside beyond there.

02:15.927 --> 02:17.303
Outside the outside of…

02:17.804 --> 02:20.598
If we get as far as possible
to the final "outside", we'll win.

02:21.349 --> 02:24.144
Win? Win what?

02:25.020 --> 02:27.647
Well, I don't know.

02:31.151 --> 02:35.822
Why did they have to
make it so hot in here?

02:38.533 --> 02:40.660
What? There are big, flying bugs!

02:40.744 --> 02:43.038
-Yikes!
-It's so hard to walk!

02:43.121 --> 02:44.205
I get it!

02:44.289 --> 02:46.166
Now it really feels like a test.

02:53.173 --> 02:56.009
That's it,
I'm going back to tell everyone.

02:56.509 --> 02:58.053
Anyway, I'm worried about Tokio.

02:58.636 --> 02:59.637
Fine.

03:00.221 --> 03:02.182
But I'm gonna keep going.

03:02.766 --> 03:03.808
Okay.

03:04.684 --> 03:05.727
What about you, Shiro?

03:11.566 --> 03:12.442
There we go.

03:12.525 --> 03:13.443
TOKIO Jr. - Jr. C

03:14.027 --> 03:18.531
These two also agree
we should return the child to Tokio.

03:18.615 --> 03:19.991
Thank you.

03:20.617 --> 03:21.785
What?

03:21.868 --> 03:23.703
How? There are two?

03:24.204 --> 03:26.873
Tokio had twins?

03:27.457 --> 03:28.792
It would seem so.

03:29.584 --> 03:32.879
Dr. Sawatari, which one
are we returning to Tokio?

03:34.172 --> 03:36.549
It's all under control. I know which one.

03:36.633 --> 03:39.511
I put a mark on one of the feet.

03:39.594 --> 03:40.929
I see.

03:41.012 --> 03:42.847
Then, the one with the mark is…

03:43.973 --> 03:47.727
That's the one we're returning to Tokio.

03:48.228 --> 03:50.146
-All right, then--
-Wait, not that one!

03:50.647 --> 03:51.690
What?

03:51.773 --> 03:53.858
So which one is it?

03:55.235 --> 04:00.740
The baby without the mark
is the one going back to Tokio!

04:03.410 --> 04:04.536
Okay, got it.

04:05.328 --> 04:08.373
-Are you okay?
-What do you mean?

04:08.456 --> 04:10.500
There's no way I'd mix them up!

04:10.583 --> 04:12.293
Of course everything is fine!

04:12.377 --> 04:15.338
No. I just meant--
You're bleeding quite a lot.

04:15.422 --> 04:18.008
-It's only a scratch!
-It is?

04:18.091 --> 04:20.802
No, I mean-- Everything is fine!

04:21.845 --> 04:25.348
Then can I leave
the one going back to Tokio with you?

04:25.432 --> 04:26.683
Yes.

04:26.766 --> 04:30.437
After I've checked
that the children are safe,

04:30.520 --> 04:33.314
if possible, I'll use this situation

04:34.190 --> 04:36.526
to execute the Noah Project.

04:37.235 --> 04:38.737
The Noah Project?

04:40.363 --> 04:44.492
What is it? Why is it called that?

04:44.576 --> 04:46.244
Does nobody know about it?

04:46.745 --> 04:47.746
I apologize.

04:48.246 --> 04:50.498
I named it in the spur of the moment.

04:52.042 --> 04:54.878
<i>It's the plan to protect the children.</i>

04:56.129 --> 04:58.048
MITA CONDO

05:00.091 --> 05:04.679
<i>It's not as if we agreed</i>
<i>exactly what day she'd be back.</i>

05:05.972 --> 05:09.017
<i>If I finally found the guy</i>
<i>I'd been searching for for five years,</i>

05:09.642 --> 05:12.062
<i>we'd probably</i>
<i>spend the whole night talking.</i>

05:13.021 --> 05:15.190
<i>I guess we'd have a few drinks--</i>

05:15.273 --> 05:16.733
<i>Well, I can't drink, but anyway.</i>

05:17.525 --> 05:21.196
<i>We'd probably end up</i>
<i>sleeping all the next day.</i>

05:22.530 --> 05:26.076
<i>But not coming back for another night</i>

05:26.951 --> 05:28.328
<i>is a little…</i>

05:30.580 --> 05:33.249
<i>Oops. The bottom's burnt.</i>

05:58.191 --> 06:00.944
-Hey you!
-You there! Stop!

06:01.027 --> 06:03.196
You can't go in there
without authorization.

06:04.197 --> 06:06.991
A woman came this way two nights ago.

06:07.534 --> 06:09.452
She hasn't returned,
so I've come to get her.

06:09.953 --> 06:14.541
What? Isn't she Inazaki's old flame?

06:14.624 --> 06:16.918
He told us not to let anyone in.

06:17.002 --> 06:19.254
Go get authorization from the Ministry.

06:19.337 --> 06:22.841
They must've rekindled their passion!

06:22.924 --> 06:26.302
I was in the plant all day yesterday,

06:26.928 --> 06:29.264
and they were just too much for me.

06:29.848 --> 06:33.351
She'll come back eventually.
Just wait a bit--

06:33.435 --> 06:36.187
Hey, you! We said no!

06:39.441 --> 06:41.026
Hey, wait…

06:42.777 --> 06:44.320
Wait!

06:55.707 --> 06:57.208
LARGE FILTRATION PLANT

06:57.292 --> 06:58.710
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

07:00.420 --> 07:02.964
Who are you? You got authorization?

07:06.134 --> 07:07.260
A bandit?

07:34.496 --> 07:36.748
<i>Since Haruki's a deep sleeper.</i>

07:40.126 --> 07:42.003
<i>What was that?</i>

07:43.254 --> 07:47.967
<i>They can't possibly be my own memories</i>
<i>of seeing myself sleeping.</i>

07:49.094 --> 07:50.136
<i>But…</i>

07:50.637 --> 07:54.849
<i>I can recall all of those memories of Sis.</i>

07:58.144 --> 08:02.774
<i>Was that one of my sister's memories</i>
<i>lingering in her body?</i>

08:04.150 --> 08:05.902
<i>She could still be alive</i>

08:06.695 --> 08:08.780
<i>somewhere in this body.</i>

08:10.448 --> 08:13.284
<i>Maybe my mind is syncing with her body</i>

08:14.119 --> 08:16.538
<i>and I'm slowly turning into my sister.</i>

08:18.123 --> 08:21.918
<i>That would be great. I'd love that.</i>

08:24.254 --> 08:26.423
It hurts.

08:27.674 --> 08:30.468
<i>What was that look on Robin's face?</i>

08:31.219 --> 08:32.887
<i>Something feels off.</i>

08:33.763 --> 08:37.434
<i>That expression he had when he saw me.</i>
<i>What did it…</i>

08:38.518 --> 08:39.644
<i>Stop.</i>

08:40.353 --> 08:42.188
<i>I don't want to think about anything.</i>

08:43.231 --> 08:45.775
<i>I just want to follow orders.</i>

08:47.527 --> 08:48.653
Like Maru.

08:51.281 --> 08:52.282
Maru!

08:52.907 --> 08:53.950
Save me!

09:00.081 --> 09:01.666
Sis?

09:03.918 --> 09:04.961
Maru!

09:20.602 --> 09:22.854
Hey! Somebody!

09:29.652 --> 09:31.446
Maru! Maru!

09:52.217 --> 09:54.969
What? You're alone?

09:55.470 --> 09:57.597
You underestimate me!

10:00.517 --> 10:02.519
I heard all about you.

10:04.145 --> 10:06.815
Aren't you the guy Haruki's guarding?

10:07.399 --> 10:09.901
Did Haruki also take care of you
down there?

10:12.654 --> 10:15.365
What the hell are you looking at?

10:39.681 --> 10:42.600
Don't mess with me, you damn kid!

11:10.045 --> 11:11.963
THE JOURNEY CONTINUES AND BEGINS

11:18.386 --> 11:20.013
Tokio? Tokio!

11:20.764 --> 11:21.765
Let me.

11:23.183 --> 11:25.143
Tokio! I'm opening the door!

11:26.644 --> 11:28.730
Tokio!

11:28.813 --> 11:29.814
Are you hurt?

11:29.898 --> 11:31.066
No.

11:31.149 --> 11:32.609
What happened?

11:33.109 --> 11:34.652
We're trying to find out.

11:34.736 --> 11:37.322
But there is something more important
I have to tell you.

11:37.989 --> 11:40.075
This baby is your child.

11:40.158 --> 11:41.159
What?

11:41.242 --> 11:43.870
This baby grew inside you.

11:43.953 --> 11:45.955
You gave birth to it, Tokio.

11:46.623 --> 11:49.167
This baby is yours and Kona's.

11:51.002 --> 11:54.798
We'll all think together
about how to raise the child,

11:55.465 --> 11:58.218
but we thought we should
at least tell you the facts.

11:58.802 --> 11:59.928
This is

12:00.553 --> 12:01.554
a baby?

12:03.598 --> 12:06.184
That thing you took out of me!

12:06.267 --> 12:07.519
Exactly.

12:07.602 --> 12:09.729
That's what all the hard work was for.

12:15.485 --> 12:16.695
So cute.

12:17.696 --> 12:19.572
Does Kona know?

12:20.073 --> 12:22.492
-We need to show Kona.
-That's right.

12:23.034 --> 12:24.994
Let's go and find him.

12:31.126 --> 12:34.337
I won't give up. Not until I win!

12:34.421 --> 12:35.672
Director!

12:35.755 --> 12:37.507
You've returned?

12:37.590 --> 12:40.385
As you can see, my timing is spot on.

12:40.885 --> 12:44.222
But wait… You can walk?

12:44.889 --> 12:46.182
Tokio!

12:46.266 --> 12:49.310
Give the baby here.

12:50.228 --> 12:51.479
Director!

12:51.563 --> 12:53.565
Let's treat your wounds first.

12:53.648 --> 12:55.650
Then I'll give you the baby.

12:55.734 --> 12:56.943
What? Never!

12:57.027 --> 12:58.695
No, Tokio!

12:58.778 --> 13:00.321
Hey, Mina!

13:00.405 --> 13:03.491
Take the baby away!

13:03.575 --> 13:05.118
<i>Understood.</i>

13:09.622 --> 13:11.750
-Please stop!
-Do it!

13:17.672 --> 13:19.299
<i>What is this?</i>

13:20.342 --> 13:22.135
<i>One of their faces is the same as yours.</i>

13:22.218 --> 13:24.220
<i>Outside of the outside?</i>

13:24.304 --> 13:25.972
There is an outside beyond here.

13:26.056 --> 13:27.891
-What are you good at?
-Run away.

13:29.434 --> 13:30.894
<i>What's happening?</i>

13:37.108 --> 13:39.611
Stay away! Nobody come near me!

13:40.153 --> 13:42.197
No, wait!

13:42.280 --> 13:43.281
<i>Kona.</i>

13:43.782 --> 13:45.033
<i>You</i>

13:45.617 --> 13:46.618
<i>and I,</i>

13:47.827 --> 13:49.454
<i>what exactly are we?</i>

14:00.215 --> 14:04.094
I thought we'd be back
at the wire fence by now.

14:04.177 --> 14:06.054
I don't see it anywhere.

14:06.554 --> 14:07.722
That's weird.

14:08.348 --> 14:11.601
We went straight ahead
and walked straight coming back, right?

14:11.685 --> 14:14.104
I thought so too.

14:14.813 --> 14:16.773
Let's keep going straight a bit more.

14:17.315 --> 14:19.317
Even if we're going
in the wrong direction…

14:19.401 --> 14:21.319
OUTSIDE OF THE OUTSIDE
WIRE FENCE - OUTSIDE - SCHOOL

14:21.403 --> 14:24.489
…if we keep going straight,
we should reach it eventually.

14:25.073 --> 14:27.492
Then we can follow the fence to get back.

14:27.575 --> 14:28.576
You're right!

14:30.787 --> 14:33.707
You're really talkative
when it's just the two of us.

14:34.290 --> 14:35.458
Am I?

14:43.842 --> 14:47.637
Hey, did we walk past a place this steep?

14:50.932 --> 14:52.392
I can hear water.

14:53.309 --> 14:55.645
I don't hear anything.

14:55.729 --> 14:56.771
Let's go see.

14:56.855 --> 15:00.567
Yeah. Anything but another tree
would make a good landmark.

15:03.820 --> 15:05.447
That's so much water.

15:05.530 --> 15:08.742
If it's flowing away from the school,

15:08.825 --> 15:10.910
then the school must be upstream.

15:10.994 --> 15:12.037
Makes sense.

15:13.788 --> 15:14.622
Mimihime!

15:33.641 --> 15:35.643
Shiro! Shiro!

15:40.273 --> 15:41.941
Stop! Don't move!

15:42.859 --> 15:43.860
Why?

15:43.943 --> 15:45.987
Why did you do that just to save me?

15:52.369 --> 15:54.704
Because I…

15:55.914 --> 15:58.416
When I think about you--

15:59.167 --> 16:01.252
Wait, no.

16:02.879 --> 16:05.131
When I think about your body--

16:05.715 --> 16:06.758
No, that's not it.

16:10.595 --> 16:14.808
I really love you, Mimihime.

16:16.768 --> 16:18.436
If it means I can save you,

16:19.688 --> 16:23.525
I don't care how many times
I get cut to shreds.

16:24.818 --> 16:27.404
If that's what you want.

16:28.446 --> 16:29.656
Or rather,

16:30.240 --> 16:31.991
if you'll let me.

17:02.814 --> 17:03.898
Stop!

17:05.442 --> 17:07.777
That's enough. Stop it.

17:08.278 --> 17:10.405
Please.

17:11.406 --> 17:12.907
Don't kill Robin.

17:40.935 --> 17:41.936
Sorry.

17:43.438 --> 17:44.689
I'm so weak.

17:45.690 --> 17:47.901
Everything I believed in was all a lie.

17:49.778 --> 17:53.823
I don't even know who I really am anymore.

17:55.283 --> 17:58.536
If you took me apart
and put me back together again,

17:58.620 --> 18:00.080
I'd probably disappear

18:01.289 --> 18:03.416
and turn into my sister instead.

18:07.671 --> 18:08.672
Sis.

18:09.422 --> 18:11.549
You've already--

18:11.633 --> 18:14.427
It feels like you've already dumped me
three or four times,

18:14.511 --> 18:16.012
but let me say it again.

18:16.638 --> 18:20.308
If you don't like it, just throw that rock
into the river and I'll stop.

18:22.686 --> 18:24.979
I'm kinda--

18:25.063 --> 18:28.692
I'm into girls.

18:29.567 --> 18:31.444
If I'd have met the real Haruki,

18:32.028 --> 18:34.239
we probably would've been friends,

18:34.739 --> 18:37.492
but I don't think
I'd have fallen for him in that way.

18:37.992 --> 18:39.953
And since you really like Kiriko,

18:40.036 --> 18:43.498
she must be a really great person.

18:43.581 --> 18:44.582
Yeah.

18:45.083 --> 18:46.918
That's one thing I'm certain of.

18:48.378 --> 18:52.215
But I don't know
if I'd have fallen for Kiriko either.

18:55.677 --> 18:56.678
Hey…

18:58.847 --> 19:00.765
you're the one I'm in love with!

19:02.308 --> 19:05.645
Not Haruki or Kiriko. It's you!

19:06.146 --> 19:07.522
You're strong!

19:07.605 --> 19:11.526
You always take care of me! And the way
you see things is always right.

19:12.068 --> 19:13.778
Without your help,

19:13.862 --> 19:18.158
<i>I wouldn't be able to drive, cook</i>
<i>or even reheat food.</i>

19:18.241 --> 19:20.535
<i>I can't do anything right without you.</i>

19:24.122 --> 19:25.999
But if you're ever in danger,

19:27.292 --> 19:28.418
I'll protect you!

19:29.878 --> 19:31.004
I'll make sure

19:31.713 --> 19:33.965
to always keep you safe.

19:35.967 --> 19:37.344
What?

19:39.262 --> 19:41.556
What's the point of my existence

19:41.639 --> 19:43.933
if I'm the one getting protected?

19:44.017 --> 19:45.101
I know, I know!

19:45.185 --> 19:46.978
You're my guard.

19:47.062 --> 19:49.564
Hey! Your snot is getting on me!

19:53.985 --> 19:56.863
When I was a kid…

19:56.946 --> 20:00.742
…I used to hiccup like this
every time I cried.

20:01.493 --> 20:03.495
It takes me back.

20:11.002 --> 20:13.963
Now I've met him
and finished what I set out to do,

20:14.589 --> 20:15.632
I don't need this.

20:24.849 --> 20:26.309
<i>Robin Inazaki,</i>

20:26.976 --> 20:30.105
<i>if I ever see you again,</i>

20:30.647 --> 20:31.898
<i>I'm going to</i>

20:32.732 --> 20:33.900
<i>kill you!</i>

20:37.404 --> 20:39.406
What do you mean nobody's here?

20:39.489 --> 20:41.241
Not sure.

20:41.324 --> 20:43.993
I couldn't get in contact
with anyone at the plant.

20:44.077 --> 20:46.830
When I came to see what was going on,
it was deserted.

20:47.747 --> 20:49.916
Is this coffee?

20:50.000 --> 20:51.710
What a waste.

20:51.793 --> 20:54.546
Sir! I found a set of keys.

20:55.672 --> 20:57.841
And those are bloodstains?

20:58.425 --> 21:00.051
What happened here?

21:01.052 --> 21:03.179
This is the only locked room.

21:03.763 --> 21:04.764
Open it.

21:08.852 --> 21:09.853
It's dark.

21:14.774 --> 21:16.609
What is that?

21:16.693 --> 21:19.654
A monster is attached to a human?

21:19.738 --> 21:20.905
That woman!

21:20.989 --> 21:24.951
I remember she registered as a resident
about three months ago.

21:25.577 --> 21:28.288
Her mind is completely gone.

21:34.627 --> 21:38.381
What the hell was Inazaki doing here?

21:51.394 --> 21:53.521
-Okay. Shall we go?
-You sure?

21:54.022 --> 21:56.566
I can't stay depressed forever.

21:57.108 --> 21:58.693
Our goal is Heaven.

21:58.777 --> 22:00.236
Our mission hasn't changed.

22:00.820 --> 22:03.740
Besides, you'll protect me
when it's dangerous, right?

22:03.823 --> 22:06.201
I will.

22:06.284 --> 22:09.996
And you'll save me when I'm in trouble.

22:17.754 --> 22:18.838
Again?

22:18.922 --> 22:22.092
It's so embarrassing to stall
just when we're making a dramatic exit!

22:22.175 --> 22:24.636
There's no one here, so it doesn't count!

22:24.719 --> 22:25.970
It's not my fault!

22:26.054 --> 22:28.014
Go complain to the Kirukomaru!
